  "date": "2026-09-23",
  "question": "When Editing + Markup deletion fully selects retained suggestion content, should the gesture stay proposed or resolve the covered pending changes and disappear from the editing view?",
  "model": "GPT-5 / Codex",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v3 with redesign-from-first-principles and Plite ownership review",
  "trigger": "A 2026-09-23 reporter video contradicts pushed commit bda11bb012: multi-block Backspace across seeded suggestions publishes a new green deletion proposal instead of removing the selected content from the editing view.",
  "requirements": [
    "Editing + Markup Backspace removes the reporter-selected multi-block content from the rendered editing view.",
    "The mounted runtime and authored mutation owner remain authoritative; no Plate or CSS workaround.",
    "A replacement resolves pending changes only when the selection fully contains each change and every required dependency.",
    "Partial retained or dependency-spanning selections preserve both content and the projected selection.",
    "Pure retained-only protection and the existing public authored intent/projection API remain intact.",
    "The previous Cmd+A, consecutive Enter, undo/redo and follow-up-input acceptance remains cumulative."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Retains the 2026-09-17 public intent/projection API, native authored authority, direction-aware mapping, history and retained-fragment owners. Reopens only the rule that every accepted-plus-pending gesture must remain proposed. Frozen bda11bb012 browser trace proves the exact runtime and semantic command execute while prepareProjectedSelectionMutation forces proposed publication. A direct accepted-range probe conflicts on retained content; complete authored decision plus accepted suffix produces the required result and one undo unit.",
  "summary": "Pursue deleting the forced proposal fallback. For an Editing + Markup replacement that fully contains every affected pending change, retained deletion and required dependency, the private projected-selection bridge accepts that closed set first, then applies the live-range replacement as the accepted suffix in the same transaction. Keep incomplete selections protected and add no public API.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-09-17-suggestions-authored-editing-final",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "reconciliation": [
    {
      "record": "2026-09-17-suggestions-authored-editing-final",
      "question": "After reconciling the decision and plan, is the authored-editing target execution-ready without another public API, state owner or unresolved product rule?",
      "action": "supersedes",
      "reason": "Retains the public API and native owners, but reporter evidence disproves the rule that a complete mixed replacement must always remain reviewable as a new proposal."
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep tx.authored.propose() for every retained-crossing selection: rejected because the exact Editing-mode gesture stays visibly present as green deletion markup.",
    "Map one accepted envelope across the retained gap: rejected as a standalone repair because the native mapper raises AuthoredMappingConflictError for retained contributions.",
    "Accept every touched change: rejected because partial fragments or dependencies outside the selection would decide unselected work.",
    "Hide retained DOM after the model delete: rejected because presentation would disagree with authored review state.",
    "Resolve the complete selected change-and-dependency set, then run the existing accepted suffix: chosen because it reuses native decisions, preserves one undo unit and keeps incomplete selections protected."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "Final implementation proof covers the package owner, exact homepage gesture, final pixels, Undo/Redo, follow-up typing, strict runtime errors and five retry-free Chromium repetitions. Cross-browser and Yjs exact-gesture replay are not claimed. The review ledger global render/check remains blocked by a pre-existing missing artifact at docs/plans/artifacts/model-api-review/document-boundary-probe.mjs.",
